# Generated from: specs/291-enforce-one-controller-writer-and-close-stale-workers/requirements.md
Feature: Enforce one controller writer and close stale workers
  Multiple controllers and prefix-matched stale workers previously wrote the same project without exact ownership.
  This was fixed by an exclusive project lease, exact worker identity, and owner-only pane cleanup.

  # --- Competing Writers Fail Closed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A foreign controller or phase helper cannot mutate a leased project
    Given canonical project P has an active controller lease for run R
    When a second execute or an unscoped verify or deliver helper starts for P
    Then it fails before changing run state, handoffs, branches, verification evidence, or pull requests
    And the active controller and its owned worker remain unchanged

  # --- Retained Ownership Is Exact ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Retained reuse requires exact worker and checkout identity
    Given run R records the expected worker name, pane, project, issue, step, branch, and head
    When execute discovers exact and prefix-colliding Herdr agents
    Then it reuses only the exact live worker whose complete ownership matches
    And an ownership mismatch fails closed without closing an unrelated pane

  # --- Owned Cleanup ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Terminal stop and cancellation close owned panes by default
    Given execute owns a worker pane under its active lease
    When the controller is cancelled or reaches a terminal non-debug stop
    Then it closes that owned pane and releases its lease
    And it keeps the pane open only when retain-worker was explicitly requested
    And unrelated panes remain open

  # --- Prompt Composition Is Unbounded ---

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Structurally valid prompts have no byte ceiling
    Given automated bodies, worker prompts, plugin fragments, builtin fragments, and project fragments are structurally valid
    When the prompt registry loads and renders them at any UTF-8 byte length
    Then no automated-body, worker-prompt, fragment, or worker-header size ceiling is enforced
    And byteBound is rejected as an unknown fragment or manifest key
    And prompt provenance, placeholders, ordering, hashes, providers, consumers, slots, source paths, and non-empty bodies remain validated
    And the controller lease, exact worker ownership, and owned-pane cleanup behavior from SCN001 through SCN003 remains unchanged
